<title>USA: Sunrise accelerates hyperopia trials.</title>
<headline>Sunrise accelerates hyperopia trials.</headline>
<dateline>FREEMONT, Calif. 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sunrise Technologies International Inc said it was accelerating enrollment in clinical trials of its holmium laser treatment for hyperopia, or farsightedness.</p>
<p>It said the move reflected interim signs that the treatment produced &quot;sustained control of regression, along with excellent long-term clinical results.&quot;</p>
<p>While other companies currently market excimer laser treatments for nearsightedness, there are none currently approved in the U.S. for farsightedness.</p>
</text>
